  - Evidence in `.reports/goal-generate-prompt-parity.md`: 60 files / 678 tests,
    typecheck clean, `npx eslint src tests` clean (plain `eslint .` hangs on the
    Windows `v1/node_modules` symlink), both drift gates green, plus a live
    built-export pass where the edited prompt alone reached the provider.
- Earlier `main` already carried the learner-delight palette/sound/motion, the
  teaching layers and the study-resilience pack.
- Working tree holds only `sessions/` churn. No server, no `out/`, `.next` or
  temp files.
- **Provider fact, proven this session:** a direct `POST` to
  `https://larprouter.com/v1/chat/completions` with `deepseek-v4.1-flash`
  returned **200** and `OK`; the browser `OPTIONS` preflight with
  `Origin: https://spanexx.github.io` returned **401 with no
  `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`**. Curl and Zed work because they are native
  clients; only browsers enforce CORS. The page cannot fix this. The real fix is
  provider-side (answer `OPTIONS` unauthenticated, then send
  `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://spanexx.github.io`,
  `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: POST, OPTIONS`,
  `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: authorization, content-type`), a relay, or a
  provider that already allows browser calls.

